      {
        "fg": "border",
        "bg": "canvas",
        "measured": {
          "light": 1.21,
          "dark": 1.36
        },
        "_note": "EXEMPT, and this is a ruling not an oversight. WCAG 2.1 SC 1.4.11 applies to graphical objects 'required to understand the content' and to UI component state. A hairline between two panes is neither: remove it entirely and every pane's content, controls and state remain fully perceivable, because the panes are already separated by their own background steps. Raising it to 3:1 would draw a hard rule around every pane and destroy the sheets-on-a-ground reading the light theme is built on. Any border that DOES carry meaning - focus, selection, validation - uses border_strong or accent, both of which are in `enforced` above.",
        "status": "exempt",
        "policy_min": 3.0
      },
