        },
        "_note": "EXEMPT, same ruling as `border`. This is the faint mid-rule inside statistical tables, the analogue of the thin rules in a typeset regression table. It groups rows; it never encodes a value. The table's numbers, headers and labels all clear 7:1 against the same surface.",
        "status": "exempt",
        "policy_min": 3.0
      }
    ],
    "_uncontrolled": "Okabe-Ito against a near-white canvas measures below 3:1 for four of eight hues in light (#F0E442 is 1.27). That is inherent to the palette and acceptable: these are data FILLS with their own outlines, never text, and 06 §14.5 adopts Okabe-Ito precisely because it is discriminable under colour-vision deficiency rather than because it is high-contrast."
